% A tsv table's fields become a fact's values under their declared types.
% A string field holds whatever bytes it decodes to, the four escapes
% included, and an integer spans the whole of int64_t with leading zeros
% and a negative zero accepted.  The table's facts join the program's own:
% an imported symbol is the same value as the one a rule names, while the
% string "plain" is not the symbol plain.
row(z, "from the program", 1).
letter(a).
letter(c).
letter(plain).
row(X, S, N)?
row(X, _, _), letter(X)?
row(_, S, _), letter(S)?
